{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q27282414","formula":"C₂₄H₄₈N₆O₁₆S₅","hill":"C24H48N6O16S5","elements":["H","C","N","O","S"],"composition":{"C":24.0,"H":48.0,"N":6.0,"O":16.0,"S":5.0},"names":{"en":"N-(2-(4-amino-N-ethyl-m-toluidino)ethyl)methanesulfonamide sesquisulfate","ru":"CD-3"},"descriptions":{"en":"The third in the series of color developing agents used in developing color films, commonly known as CD-3, is chemically known as N-[2-[(4-Amino-3-methylphenyl)ethylamino]ethyl]methanesulfonamide Sesquisulfate Monohydrate. In color development, after reducing a silver atom in a silver halide crystal, the oxidized developing agent combines with a color coupler to form a color dye molecule. CD-3 is used in many processes including VNF-1, ECN-2 and the E-6 process.","ru":"CD-3 (N-этил-N-метиленсульфонаминоэтил-3-метил-п-фенилендиамин сесквисульфат, 2-амино-5-[N-этил-N-(β-метилсульфонамидоэтил)]-аминотолуолсульфонат моногидрат) — органическое соединение с формулой C24H48N6O16S5. Используется как цветное проявляющее вещество паратолуилендиаминового ряда в фотографии. CD-3 — торговое название, использующееся фирмой Kodak и являющееся сокращением от Color Developing Agent 3 (цветное проявляющее вещество 3)."},"fame":6,"pubchemCid":91578,"mass":837.0,"charge":0,"smiles":"CCN(CCNS(=O)(=O)C)C1=CC(=C(C=C1)N)C.CCN(CCNS(=O)(=O)C)C1=CC(=C(C=C1)N)C.OS(=O)(=O)O.OS(=O)(=O)O.OS(=O)(=O)O","inchikey":"NPDFXFLCEDDWEG-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"bis(N-[2-(4-amino-N-ethyl-3-methylanilino)ethyl]methanesulfonamide);sulfuric acid","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"91578","atoms":99,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-0.486,"y":-2.482,"z":-0.045,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.113,"y":-1.642,"z":1.057,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.798,"y":-0.218,"z":0.851,"el":"N"},{"x":0.464,"y":0.256,"z"